# Default handling: let Git normalize text files in the repository.
* text=auto

# The shipped report records the SHA256 of the manifest it ran against, and that
# manifest is samples/lab-intent.json. Line-ending normalization would change its
# bytes and break the check on any platform whose native ending differs from the
# one it was written with. Stored verbatim, with no conversion in either direction.
samples/lab-intent.json -text

# Same reasoning for the report: it carries the hash it must agree with, and a
# diff on it should reflect a different run, not a different platform.
samples/output.json -text

# samples/intent.json is a hand-written format example. Nothing hashes it, so it
# follows normal text handling.
